{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>A man of the soil.</b> That remained for him and his sons, and that returned to yield its strength to him, as I explained above." "<b>And he planted a vineyard.</b> He brought with him vine-cuttings and fig saplings. Because they spoil in water more than other trees. Another interpretation: HaShem said to him, 'of every food that you shall eat' — and bundles of cuttings are food for livestock. Another interpretation: because the seeds of these two trees are not suited for planting like the seeds of other trees."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {1 "The acronym פרש״י in this compiler's text is written with a resh, the standard reverent substitution; it refers to Rashi's commentary. The phrase מאכל פילין (food for livestock/working animals) is rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:40.508537312Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}